  <Properties>
    <pitchId>
      <Value><![CDATA[mobilepay-for-toddlers]]></Value>
    </pitchId>
    <title>
      <Value><![CDATA[MobilePay for Toddlers]]></Value>
    </title>
    <tagline>
      <Value><![CDATA[Send 3 raisins to Alma. Swipe with your whole hand.]]></Value>
    </tagline>
    <demoFeatures>
      <Value><![CDATA[Raisin Transfer
Snack Split
Lunchbox Wallet
Nap Cashback]]></Value>
    </demoFeatures>
    <cardsEpic>
      <Value><![CDATA[Cashless sandbox by 2027 | Replace all sand-based payments. A sand cake is not legal tender, whatever the Red Room says.
Disrupt the raisin economy | Raisins are the incumbent currency. We go after the whole market, including the tiny red boxes.
Global toddler onboarding | Onboard every three-year-old in the Nordics. KYC now stands for Know Your Kid.
Pocket Money as a Service | Recurring revenue from parents. Churn happens automatically when the user turns six.
Seed round from the grandparents | Raise from four grandparents. Valuation: 'so clever for her age'. Term sheet: a banknote in a card.
Sandbox-to-production pipeline | Our sandbox environment is an actual sandbox. Prod is the slide. There is no staging.]]></Value>
    </cardsEpic>
    <cardsStory>
      <Value><![CDATA[Pay by pacifier | As a toddler, I want to pay with my pacifier so that I never have to remember a PIN.
Split the Friday sweets | As a four-year-old, I want to split the Friday sweets 50/50 so that I get the big half.
Parental approval | As a dad, I want to approve every purchase so that I can say no on two platforms at once.
Trade regret refund | As a toddler, I want to undo the trade so that I get the red spade back and also keep the bucket.
Nap time settlement | As a kindergarten teacher, I want all debts settled before nap time so that nobody sleeps as a creditor.
Three-digit PIN | As a three-year-old, I want my PIN to be 1-2-3 so that it ends where the numbers end.
Grandma top-up | As a grandma, I want to send money without Mum knowing so that I remain the favourite.
Tantrum-proof checkout | As a product owner, I want checkout to survive a meltdown in aisle four so that conversion holds.
Request money, loudly | As a toddler, I want to request money by shouting MINE so that the UX matches my current workflow.
Lunchbox exchange | As a five-year-old, I want to swap my rye bread for anything at all so that the market finally clears.
Billable nap time | As a project manager, I want nap time logged as billable so that the kindergarten hits its utilisation.
The client's nephew, aged 4 | As the client's nephew, I want admin access so that I can build it myself, like my uncle said I could.]]></Value>
    </cardsStory>
    <cardsFeature>
      <Value><![CDATA[Fingerpaint ID | Biometric login with fingerpaint. Works best in blue.
Sticky finger mode | Detects jam on the screen and enlarges every button to 400 px.
Raisin wallet | Hold your balance in raisins. The exchange rate is set by the biggest kid.
Sticker cashback | One glitter sticker per payment. It goes on the screen. Then on the dog.
Emoji-only receipts | The receipt is three emojis. Nobody here can read anyway.
Peekaboo privacy mode | Cover your eyes and your balance disappears. Bank-grade.
Sand cake invoicing | Send an invoice for one sand cake. Payment terms: now.
'But why?' confirmation flow | The app asks 'but why?' five times before any transfer. Revenge is sweet.
Nap time maintenance window | The system is down from 12 to 2. Shh.
No-take-backs lock | A trade is final once both parties have said 'no take-backs'. Legally binding in the cloakroom.
Snowsuit mode | A UI you can use with mittens on. One button. It is big.
Playdate subscriptions | Recurring playdate, auto-renews every Thursday until somebody bites.
Snack-time surge pricing | Raisin prices triple at 2 pm. The market is ruthless and it is three years old.
Tooth fairy payouts | Instant settlement, with the tooth held as collateral under the pillow.
Sharing mode | Splits every payment with the nearest child. Cannot be switched off. It builds character.
Count-to-ten rate limiter | Max ten transactions, then the system counts again. It skips seven.]]></Value>
    </cardsFeature>
    <cardsBug>
      <Value><![CDATA[User ate the payment terminal | Steps: hand terminal to user. Expected: payment. Actual: chewing sounds. Priority: high chair.
Balance shows 'lots' | Every amount over 3 displays as 'lots'. Matches the user's mental model. Won't fix?
Transfer sent to 14 Mums | 14 users have a contact called Mum. The money went to the wrong Mum. All of them.
Session expires during nappy change | User comes back logged out, furious and in new trousers.
Duplicate charge on 'AGAIN!' | User shouts 'again!' and the payment retries forever. The idempotency key is a teddy.
Refund loop between twins | The twins refund each other in an infinite loop. Works on my playroom.
Scream parsed as voice command | A 110 dB scream approved a transfer of 400 raisins. Cannot reproduce without earplugs.
Rounding error: half a biscuit | System rounds down. User noticed. User always notices. Severity: meltdown.]]></Value>
    </cardsBug>
    <cardsTechdebt>
      <Value><![CDATA[Ledger is a drawing on the fridge | The entire transaction ledger is in crayon. Backup strategy: Grandma took a photo.
Auth is 'are you a grown-up?' | Login asks if you are an adult and trusts the answer. Since 2019.
Bedtime hardcoded in 43 places | 7 pm, everywhere. Daylight saving breaks everything, including the children.
Tests written in crayon | Unit tests exist, but in crayon, and somebody has eaten the green one.
Variables: var1, var2, teddy | Core payment module. Nobody dares rename teddy.
Prod hotfix is a dinosaur plaster | Applied in 2021 as a temporary fix. It holds. Do not touch it.]]></Value>
    </cardsTechdebt>
    <cardsCeo>
      <Value><![CDATA[CEO Request: Can toddlers pay invoices? | 'They have no money, sure, but so much potential as a segment.'
CEO Request: AI in the sandbox | 'I saw something on LinkedIn.' No further spec. Deadline: the julefrokost.
CEO Request: Where is the B2B angle? | 'Baby to baby. B2B. You can have that one for free.' Then the lift doors closed.]]></Value>
    </cardsCeo>
    <siteHeroHeadline>
      <Value><![CDATA[Pay with one swipe. And a bit of jam.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroHeadline>
    <siteHeroSub>
      <Value><![CDATA[The payment app for users who can't read, count or let go of the phone. Send raisins, request stickers, split the Friday sweets. Mostly fairly.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroSub>
    <siteCta>
      <Value><![CDATA[Send a raisin]]></Value>
    </siteCta>
    <sitePillars>
      <Value><![CDATA[Tested in sandbox | An actual sandbox. Our QA team is four years old and found 212 bugs. They ate nine of them.
Bank-grade safety | Protected by fingerpaint ID and a teacher with eyes in the back of their head. No transfers during nap time.
No reading required | The whole UI is three colours and one big button. Also our most requested feature among senior stakeholders.]]></Value>
    </sitePillars>
    <siteTestimonials>
      <Value><![CDATA[MINE! (Translated by our onboarding team: 'intuitive and best in class'.)
My daughter sent 400 raisins to a boy called Storm. We have never met Storm.
I'm a kindergarten teacher. I now have a four-year-old CFO. She is strict but fair.
He paid for his own pacifier. I have never been prouder or more worried.]]></Value>
    </siteTestimonials>
    <sitePricingJoke>
      <Value><![CDATA[Free up to age three. After that, one sticker per transaction. Glitter stickers count double.]]></Value>
    </sitePricingJoke>
    <siteFooterLine>
      <Value><![CDATA[© MobilePay for Toddlers. Not a bank. Not a kindergarten. Please fetch a grown-up.]]></Value>
    </siteFooterLine>
